.TH SDL_HINT_WAVE_CHUNK_LIMIT 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_WAVE_CHUNK_LIMIT \- A variable controlling the maximum number of chunks in a WAVE file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_WAVE_CHUNK_LIMIT \(dqSDL_WAVE_CHUNK_LIMIT\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This sets an upper bound on the number of chunks in a WAVE file to avoid wasting time on malformed or corrupt WAVE files\[char46] This defaults to \(dq10000\(dq\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before calling
.BR SDL_LoadWAV ()
or
.BR SDL_LoadWAV_IO ()

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

